{{Quote|You will, therefore, be taken to the Dune Sea and cast into the Pit of Carkoon, the nesting place of the all-powerful sarlacc.|C-3PO, translating Jabba the Hutt|<ref name="Episode VI" />}}
The '''Great Pit of Carkoon''', also known as the '''Sarlacc Pit''', was a large sand basin located within the [[Dune Sea]], on the [[desert]] [[planet]] of [[Tatooine]].<ref name="RotJ novel">[[Star Wars: Return of the Jedi (paperback novel)|''Star Wars: Return of the Jedi'' junior novelization]]</ref> The pit was home to the "[[almighty Sarlacc]]," who was an unusually non-carnivorous [[sarlacc]] and did not appreciate sentients being force-fed to it.<ref name="FACPOV">{{StoryCite|story=My Mouth Never Closes|book=From a Certain Point of View: Return of the Jedi}}</ref> Like other sarlaccs, its digestion could take [[Millennium|thousands]] of [[Standard year|years]]. Due to its proximity to [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]]'s [[Boba Fett's Palace|palace]], the [[crime lord]] used the pit and its sarlacc for [[Torture|torturous]] executions. The pit was the location of the [[rescue of Han Solo]], which took place shortly before the [[Battle of Endor]]. Jabba was killed next to the Great Pit of Carkoon in the ''[[Khetanna]]'' by [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]].<ref name="Episode VI" /> The pit, alongside the sarlacc inhabiting it, was later destroyed when [[Fennec Shand]] dropped one of ''[[Slave I]]''{{'s}} [[seismic charge]]s into it.<ref name="GatheringStorm">{{BOBF|Chapter 4: The Gathering Storm}}</ref>

{{Nature-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The sound of the sarlacc was created from sounds of alligator hisses, as well as the sounds of some of the [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Return of the Jedi'']] crew's stomachs after eating pizza.<ref name="Drawing from the Present: Familiar Creatures in a Galaxy Far, Far Away">{{SW|url=news/drawing-from-the-present-familiar-creatures-in-a-galaxy-far-far-away|text=Drawing from the Present: Familiar Creatures in a Galaxy Far, Far Away|int=Back from the Drawing Board|nolive=1}}</ref>

